 "about": "lib/printer-success.js successRates(input): per printer, finished / (finished + failed) from run results (P6). Synthetic book. A case with `calendar: { utcOffsetMinutes }` passes `dayOf` = that fixed-offset calendar's day of the run's `at` (a full UTC stamp shifted by the offset; a bare YYYY-MM-DD returned as written). Without it, the lib's own fallback: the first ten characters. Or `calendar: { timeZone }` (an IANA zone id): dayOf is that zone's local day, daylight saving included; a single fixed offset fails those cases, which is the point of them.",
